        <mxCell id="c78" value="Notation&lt;br&gt;Unmarked use cases are realised in both the API and the web portal.&lt;br&gt;API only — implemented and tested in the API, not yet offered by&lt;br&gt;the web portal: UC12 Release Pickup, UC13 Cancel Donation,&lt;br&gt;UC26 Manage User Accounts.&lt;br&gt;Include and extend conditions&lt;br&gt;UC01 «include» UC02 — signing up as an NGO always creates a Recipient;&lt;br&gt;as a courier, a Volunteer. The role admin is refused by SELF_SIGNUP_ROLES.&lt;br&gt;UC05, UC07 «include» UC14 — ranking always runs when a donation is&lt;br&gt;posted, and again when it is first accepted, to freeze the score the&lt;br&gt;decision was made on.&lt;br&gt;UC15 «extend» UC06 — condition: the donation is still AVAILABLE or&lt;br&gt;MATCHED and the caller's account is bound to a recipient organisation.&lt;br&gt;Guards and overrides not drawn as relationships&lt;br&gt;UC07 — the accepting organisation must already be verified by an&lt;br&gt;administrator, otherwise acceptance is refused with 403.&lt;br&gt;UC27 — an administrator is admitted by every entry of TRANSITION_ROLES&lt;br&gt;and so may drive UC07 and UC12 on another party's behalf.&lt;br&gt;The first administrator exists only via the command line&lt;br&gt;(python -m foodlink.cli create-admin); every later one via UC26." style="rounded=0;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#8A7F72;fontSize=10;spacingLeft=6;spacingTop=2;" parent="1" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry x="360" y="1831" width="476" height="402" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
  </diagram>
</mxfile>
